claude-nerf-watcher — https://github.com/One-Lyf/claude-nerf-watcher
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Used as a reference (commit bf7a533). The limit-health method in
src/shared/usage/health.ts is adapted from nerf.py: scoring each 5-hour window
as API-equivalent dollars per 1% of the limit, pricing a model family at one
rate, the median baseline over trusted dates stored per 1x of plan, the plan
history with pro/max5/max20/custom multipliers, the "N low windows in a row
below baseline ÷ threshold" flag (defaults 1.5 and 2), skipping windows under
10%, showing each window's token mix, and backfilling readings from old
transcripts (src/shared/usage/usage-command.ts). The app does not read
Claude's OAuth token or call the usage endpoint nerf-watcher relies on; its
percentages come only from the status line bridge and recorded /usage output.

